    "content": "Today, March 20/21, 2026, Muslims are celebrating Eid al-Fitr, the \"Feast of Fast-Breaking,\" marking the end of the holy month of Ramadan. It is a major three-day celebration involving early morning prayers, charity (Zakat al-Fitr), wearing new clothes, and sharing feasts with family and friends. Key Details About Today's Holiday: Significance: Celebrates the completion of a month of fasting, spiritual reflection, and increased devotion. Common Traditions: Eid Prayers: Special communal prayers held early in the morning. Charity: Zakat al-Fitr (or Fitrana) is given to the poor to ensure they can participate in the celebration. Festivities: Visiting family and friends, giving gifts (often money to children), and wearing new clothes. Food: Known as the \"Sweet Festival\" for the special desserts and treats made to celebrate. Greetings: \"Eid Mubarak\" (Blessed Eid) or \"Eid Sa'id\" (Happy Eid). Note: The exact date of Eid al-Fitr can vary slightly based on local sightings of the crescent moon.",
